From d21fd152031766f4e7c39feeacb7af7289863fad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iwanicki92 <iwanicki92@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 18:46:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] slaunch: read the Linux MLE header at the offset kernel_info
 gives

sl_efi_load_mle_data() reads mle_header_offset from kernel_info into a
local, then dereferences slparams->mle_header_offset instead, which is
still zero on the EFI path. The "header" it finds is the bzImage's MZ
stub, whose bytes at the entry_point offset are zero, and the UUID check
is inverted so the mismatch passes. slparams->mle_entry ends up 0.

TXT never reads mle_entry, the ACM takes the entry from the MLE header
itself, so Intel EFI boots hid this. On AMD the SLRT's dlme_entry is
mle_entry, so SKL jumps to startup_32 rather than sl_stub_entry. The
kernel then boots without SLAUNCH_FLAG, never runs
slaunch_cpu_setup_skinit() and its STGI, and with GIF still clear from
SKINIT no interrupt is ever delivered: check_timer() panics with "timer
doesn't work through Interrupt-remapped IO-APIC". The legacy path sets
mle_entry from the header it seeks to in the file and boots.

Point at the header the offset names, relative to the protected-mode
kernel like kernel_info_offset is, and fail when the UUID does not match.

Signed-off-by: iwanicki92 <iwanicki92@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 grub-core/loader/slaunch/x86_efi_linux.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/grub-core/loader/slaunch/x86_efi_linux.c b/grub-core/loader/slaunch/x86_efi_linux.c
index f1c2c1d..2a457ae 100644
--- a/grub-core/loader/slaunch/x86_efi_linux.c
+++ b/grub-core/loader/slaunch/x86_efi_linux.c
@@ -120,12 +120,12 @@ sl_efi_load_mle_data (struct grub_slaunch_params *slparams,
         }
 
       mle_hdr_offset = grub_le_to_cpu32 (kernel_info.mle_header_offset);
-      mle_hdr = (struct grub_txt_mle_header *)((grub_addr_t)kernel_addr + slparams->mle_header_offset);
+      mle_hdr = (struct grub_txt_mle_header *)((grub_addr_t)kernel_addr + kernel_start + mle_hdr_offset);
 
-      if (!grub_memcmp (mle_hdr->uuid, GRUB_TXT_MLE_UUID, 16))
+      if (grub_memcmp (mle_hdr->uuid, GRUB_TXT_MLE_UUID, 16) != 0)
         {
           grub_dprintf ("slaunch", "Not an MLE header at %llu\n",
-                        (unsigned long long)((grub_addr_t)kernel_addr + mle_hdr_offset));
+                        (unsigned long long)(grub_addr_t)mle_hdr);
           return GRUB_ERR_BAD_OS;
         }
     }
